{"method_version":"monitor-1.2","generated_utc":"2026-11-25T00:07:22Z","data_cutoff_utc":"2026-11-25T00:00:00Z","disclaimer":"Descriptive only, not a forecast. These numbers describe aftershocks recorded between each mainshock and the data cut-off. They do not give the probability or the number of future earthquakes. For official aftershock forecasts, see the USGS event pages and the national agencies of the affected countries.","selection":{"min_mag":7.0,"default_min_mag":7.0,"fallback_min_mag":6.5,"fallback_used":false,"window_days":365,"query_minmag":2.5,"catalogue":"USGS ComCat, as served"},"method":"Sequence Monitor: a descriptive, regularly updated summary of ongoing large-earthquake aftershock sequences.\n\nNOT A FORECAST. Every number describes events between a mainshock and the data cut-off. No probability, no\nexpected future count and no curve beyond the cut-off is produced. The USGS runs operational aftershock forecasts\n(the ComCat `oaf` product); this monitor only describes what has happened so far.\n\nSelection : ComCat mainshocks M >= 7.0 in the 365 days before the cut-off (M >= 6.5 if fewer than 5 are found).\n            Largest first; an event inside the window of a larger mainshock (0-365 days after, within R), or a\n            doublet within 1 day and 2 R of it, joins that sequence instead of starting its own.\nWindow    : epicentral radius R = max(100 km, 10^(-2.44 + 0.59 M)) (Wells & Coppersmith 1994, the atlas rule),\n            depth within 100 km of the mainshock depth, from the mainshock to the cut-off. ComCat events M >= 2.5,\n            as served (mixed magnitude types); a query above ComCat's 20,000-event limit is repeated at M >= 3.5,\n            then split in time.\nMcat      : MAXC + 0.2 of the events after min(10 days, half the sequence age); 4.5 if fewer than 30 such events.\nMc(t)     : max(Mcat, Mm - 4.5 - 0.75 log10 t) (Helmstetter et al. 2006; Page et al. 2016).\nOmori     : Omori-Utsu MLE above Mc(t) (seislib.omori_fit_mct), b = sequence b-positive if >= 50 differences, else 1.\n            95 % intervals from the observed information (K with its covariance with p and c); c >= 1e-4 day;\n            quality A/B/C as in the atlas sequence fits.\nb         : binned maximum likelihood (Tinti & Mulargia 1987) with the per-event threshold Mc(t); 1000 bootstrap\n            resamples with Mcat re-estimated; shown only for quality A (95 % interval width / b <= 0.30) or B (<= 0.50)\n            with >= 50 events. b-positive (van der Elst 2021) on the events at or above Mcat.\nZW2020    : optional, subduction-zone regimes only: count above Mc(t) divided by the direct-aftershock count above\n            Mc(t) of the Zhang & Werner (2020) Table 6 ETAS parameters over the same span, next to the same ratio\n            (also above Mc(t)) for their own Case 3 sequences (descriptive; nothing is extrapolated past the cut-off).\nProductivity : sequence a-value with p, c, b fixed at the generic values of Page et al. (2016) for the Garcia et\n            al. (2012) tectonic region of the epicentre, compared with the regional distribution of a (mean,\n            sigma). \"more\" / \"less\" only when the whole 95 % interval of the sequence a lies above the 75th /\n            below the 25th percentile of the regional distribution (mean +/- 0.6745 sigma); otherwise \"typical\".","references":{"page2016":"Page, M. T., van der Elst, N., Hardebeck, J., Felzer, K., Michael, A. J. (2016), BSSA 106(5), 2290-2301, doi:10.1785/0120160073","zw2020":"Zhang, L., Werner, M. J., Goda, K. (2020), BSSA 110(1), 191-212, doi:10.1785/0120190121 (Table 6 ETAS parameters; Table 2 Case 3 counts as the reference ratios)","regimes":"Garcia, D., Wald, D. J., Hearne, M. G. (2012), BSSA 102(1), 185-203; grid from OpenSHA OAF (github.com/opensha/opensha-oaf)"},"sequences":[{"id":"us6000u43g","time":"2026-10-22T14:33:40Z","lat":32.338,"lon":93.784,"depth":18.0,"mag":7.0,"magtype":"mww","place":"189 km ENE of Nagqu, China","url":"ht